      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "App routing eagerly imports several heavy tool pages, pulling large dependency trees into initial load.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "dependency_health",
        "related_files": [
          "src/app/routes.tsx",
          "src/tools/join-clips/pages/JoinClipsPage.tsx",
          "src/shared/components/MediaGallery/index.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`routes.tsx` eagerly imports `ImageGenerationToolPage`, `VideoTravelToolPage`, `CharacterAnimatePage`, `JoinClipsPage`, and `EditVideoPage`.",
          "`JoinClipsPage.tsx` itself has broad imports across gallery/lightbox/hooks, compounding route-level eager load weight.",
          "`MediaGallery/index.tsx` is a high-dependency component used in tool pages and contributes to transitive bundle expansion when tool routes are eager."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Restore lazy loading for primary tool routes with a guarded hydration-ready boundary (e.g., defer mount until query/runtime bootstrap signal) so Safari workaround does not require full eager imports.",
        "reasoning": ""
