      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Media gallery item behavior is fragmented across prop-bag orchestration surfaces.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "high_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/components/MediaGalleryItem/components/ShotActions.tsx",
          "src/shared/components/MediaGallery/hooks/useMediaGalleryHandlers.ts",
          "src/shared/components/MediaGalleryItem/hooks/useMediaGalleryItemState.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`ShotActions.tsx` requires large grouped props (`selector`, `status`, `quickCreate`, `actions`) and embeds navigation/add business branching in UI component code.",
          "`useMediaGalleryHandlers.ts` duplicates related action concerns (navigate, notifier jump, modal transitions) that are part of the same gallery-item interaction lifecycle.",
          "`useMediaGalleryItemState.ts` owns additional workflow state and async create-shot error flow, further splitting one interaction domain across multiple modules."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce a single `useMediaGalleryItemController` (or equivalent) that owns shot-action workflow and exposes a smaller view model to presentational components.",
        "reasoning": ""
