      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Generation identity changes across seams, causing task lookups to use the wrong ID type in fallback paths.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/lib/generationTransformers.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/generationTaskCache.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/generationTaskRepository.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`transformForTimeline` sets `id` to `shotGen.id` and allows `generation_id` to remain nullable.",
          "`enhanceGenerationsWithTaskData` computes `generationId = generation.generation_id ?? generation.id` and uses that key for `taskQueryKeys.generationMapping(...)`.",
          "`getPrimaryTaskMappingsForGenerations` queries `generations` by `.in('id', requestedIds)`, so a fallback `shot_generations.id` will always miss and be treated as mapping failure."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make `generation_id` mandatory for timeline-transformed rows (or reject rows without it), and remove the `?? generation.id` fallback in task mapping enrichment so only canonical generation IDs cross the repository boundary.",
        "reasoning": ""
