        "evidence": [
          "Holistic structure shows `src/shared/components/ui/` has 58 files and includes primitives, hooks, setup files, and tests in one folder.",
          "`cn.ts` in UI is a facade over shared lib implementation, while `button.tsx` depends on theme variants in another package, indicating blurred package contracts.",
          "Coupling data shows very high inbound usage of the UI directory, so unclear organization amplifies codebase-wide navigation cost."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Execute a staged reorg plan: (1) create target folders `src/shared/components/ui/primitives/`, `src/shared/components/ui/hooks/`, `src/shared/components/ui/adapters/`, and `src/shared/components/ui/__tests__/`; (2) move files in order: hooks/util adapters first (`cn.ts`, tooltip hooks), then primitive components (`button.tsx` and peers), then tests; (3) run import updates with `rg \"@/shared/components/ui/\" -n src | head` and a codemod or scripted path replace; (4) validate with `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test`, and `npm run lint`.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
