    "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::task_payload_canonical_contract_not_enforced::e9747424": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::task_payload_canonical_contract_not_enforced::e9747424",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Video-travel task display and execution still depend on multi-path fallback chains instead of a single canonical payload contract.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "abstraction_fitness",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/components/TaskDetails/VideoTravelDetails.tsx",
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/individualTravelSegment.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/travelBetweenImages/payloadBuilder.ts",
          "supabase/functions/complete_task/orchestrator.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`VideoTravelDetails` repeatedly resolves each field from 3-4 alternative locations (e.g. phase config, motion mode, prompts, structure guidance, preset, frames) across `individual_segment_params`, `orchestrator_payload`, `orchestrator_details`, and parsed root params.",
          "`individualTravelSegment` reconstructs runtime state using layered fallbacks from `originalParams` and nested `orchestrator_details` for seed, loras, mode flags, model, and flow settings, indicating the contract is not trusted as singular.",
          "`orchestrator.ts` sibling queries still support multiple run-id/orchestrator-id key locations (`params->>run_id`, `params->orchestrator_details->>run_id`, etc.), which is another compatibility layer for drifted schemas."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Define one canonical persisted schema for travel/join task metadata (contract-first), migrate builders to write only that shape, and move all readers to a single adapter that normalizes old payloads once at ingress before business logic/UI rendering.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Disappeared from scan \u2014 likely fixed",
