        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/calculate-task-cost/index.ts",
          "supabase/functions/complete_task/orchestrator.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "In `calculate-task-cost`, sub-task query binds `error` to `_subTasksError` and never branches on it.",
          "When that query errors, logic falls through to the \"regular task\" duration path (`else`) instead of returning an explicit billing-read failure.",
          "This creates inconsistent semantics versus other DB reads in the same function (`existingSpendError`, `taskTypeError`, `ledgerError`) that are explicitly handled."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Treat sub-task query failures as first-class errors: check `subTasksError`, log context, and return a recoverable error response instead of billing as if no sub-tasks existed.",
