        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/complete_task/orchestrator.ts",
          "supabase/functions/calculate-task-cost/index.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`markOrchestratorComplete` throws for task update failures, but after completion it only `console.error`s when `triggerCostCalculation(...).ok` is false.",
          "This means the task is finalized as `Complete` even when billing fails, creating non-uniform failure handling inside a single completion transaction.",
          "`calculate-task-cost` itself returns explicit structured errors for multiple failure conditions, indicating billing is expected to be reliability-critical."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make billing failure policy explicit and consistent: either propagate billing failure (and mark orchestrator failed/retryable) or persist an explicit \"billing_pending/billing_failed\" state that downstream reconciliation can enforce.",
