      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Supabase lookup errors are silently downgraded to fallback/no-op paths",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/ShotImagesEditor/hooks/useShotImagesEditorCallbacks.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/individualTravelSegment.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`useShotImagesEditorCallbacks` fetches `beforeData` (`.single()`) and returns when `!beforeData` (line 62) without checking the query error, and sibling lookup (`siblings`) also proceeds without inspecting error before deriving `idsToDelete`.",
          "`createIndividualTravelSegmentTask` checks `!pairIdError && childByPairId` and `!orderError && childByOrder`, but any lookup error is otherwise ignored, causing error cases to be treated the same as \"not found\"."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Normalize lookup boundaries to one contract: explicitly handle query errors (wrap with `handleAndRethrow`/domain error and context), and keep fallback behavior only for true not-found results. Distinguish \"lookup failed\" from \"lookup empty\" in both modules.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
