    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::lossy_error_adapters::6357d0c1": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::lossy_error_adapters::6357d0c1",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Adapter layers drop structured failure details into primitives",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/ShotImagesEditor/hooks/useShotImagesEditorCallbacks.ts",
          "src/pages/Home/hooks/useDiscordSignIn.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`useShotImagesEditorCallbacks` internal operations return `OperationResult` with policy/error metadata, but `handleAddToShotAdapter` and `handleAddToShotWithoutPositionAdapter` return only `false` on failure, and `handleCreateShotAdapter` returns `undefined`, discarding failure context.",
          "`useDiscordSignIn` returns full `OperationResult` to callers, preserving `errorCode`, `policy`, and recoverability details; this contrast creates inconsistent caller expectations for handling failures across action hooks."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Standardize exported async action hooks to return a single error contract (prefer `OperationResult` end-to-end). If compatibility adapters must remain, add explicit typed \"legacy\" naming and expose parallel non-lossy variants so callers can opt into consistent structured handling.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
