          "src/tools/edit-images/hooks/useInlineEditState.ts",
          "src/tools/edit-images/components/InlineEditView.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`VideoLightbox.tsx` composes mode/environment/shared/edit/render models, then forwards assembled props to `LightboxLayout`, creating several intermediate abstraction layers with little domain reduction.",
          "`useVideoLightboxRenderModel.tsx` carries a large dependency/pass-through surface to build panel content and layout props, increasing indirection for simple UI changes.",
          "Inline edit replicates similar orchestration and control surfaces (`useInlineEditState` + `InlineEditView`) while reusing low-level lightbox components, suggesting boundary duplication rather than a stable shared view model."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Collapse to one feature-level controller per mode (image/video/edit) that exposes a minimal, stable view contract to layout components, and extract shared edit-control primitives once for both lightbox and inline-edit paths to reduce pass-through seams.",
        "reasoning": ""
