        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/ShotImagesEditor/hooks/useShotImagesEditorCallbacks.ts",
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/ShotImagesEditor/hooks/useSegmentSlotMode.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`handleDeleteSegment` throws on failure via `handleAndRethrow` (`useShotImagesEditorCallbacks.ts:149-153`), while sibling operations (`runAddToShotOperation`, `runAddToShotWithoutPositionOperation`, `runCreateShotOperation`) catch errors and return `operationFailure` (`:215-221`, `:247-253`, `:287-293`).",
          "This creates different caller obligations for closely related actions in the same hook surface: some paths require try/catch, others require `result.ok` branching."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pick one failure contract for this callback family (prefer `OperationResult` for UI event handlers), refactor `handleDeleteSegment` to return `OperationResult` instead of throwing, and align callers such as segment-slot handlers to one consistent pattern.",
