          "`useInlineEditState` returns a very large nested object (`canvasEnvironment`, `inpaintingState`, `transformState`, `generationState`, `imageEditValue`) and also defines additional projection types (`InlineEditCanvasState`, `InlineEditSidebarState`).",
          "`useInlineEditViewState` immediately calls `useInlineEditState` and remaps fields via `selectInlineEditCanvasState`/`selectInlineEditSidebarState`, adding an extra wrapper layer without reducing dependency surface.",
          "`InlineEditView` mostly forwards this mapped state to `InlineEditCanvas`/`InlineEditSidebar` and then to `EditModePanel`, preserving high coupling across the chain."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Refactor inline edit to expose a smaller command-oriented API per concern (canvas, generation actions, sidebar actions) and let leaf components consume dedicated hooks/context directly. Remove `useInlineEditViewState` as a pass-through layer once slices are independently consumable.",
