    "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::legacy_supabase_parallel_surface_still_primary::487dd44a": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::legacy_supabase_parallel_surface_still_primary::487dd44a",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Legacy Supabase facade remains a parallel primary client surface across modules instead of a narrow end-stage shim.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "cross_module_architecture",
        "related_files": [
          "src/integrations/supabase/legacy/legacySupabaseFacade.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/toolConstants.ts",
          "README.md"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`legacySupabaseFacade.ts` exports `supabase` as a live compatibility facade with multiple core client members, not a narrow migration-only shim.",
          "The facade still includes active lifecycle governance fields (`LEGACY_SUPABASE_IMPORT_BUDGET`, removal date), indicating ongoing cross-module usage pressure rather than near-retirement.",
          "This preserves two architectural entrypaths (`getSupabaseClient()` vs legacy `supabase`) and weakens dependency-direction discipline.",
          "The facade still exports `supabase` with broad data/auth/storage/realtime/functions accessors and call proxies (`from`, `rpc`, `channel`), so callers can continue avoiding canonical runtime access APIs.",
          "`LEGACY_SUPABASE_IMPORT_BUDGET = 129` and README governance text explicitly permit substantial ongoing imports before 2026-06-30."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Collapse compatibility to a single transitional accessor (preferably only `getLegacySupabaseClient`), reduce allowed members to the minimum migration set, and enforce a sharply descending budget schedule (not a static high cap) so boundary convergence is measurable each release.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Disappeared from scan \u2014 likely fixed",
