    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::join_clips_storage_fallback_masks_corruption::91fd2856": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::join_clips_storage_fallback_masks_corruption::91fd2856",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Join Clips storage helpers silently swallow localStorage failures and malformed cache values, creating unobservable degraded behavior.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/join-clips/lib/clipInitService.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/pages/JoinClipsPage.tsx",
          "src/pages/Home/hooks/useDiscordSignIn.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`getCachedClipsCount` catches all errors and returns `0` (`clipInitService.ts:36-41`), while `setCachedClipsCount` also uses silent `catch {}` (`clipInitService.ts:46-54`).",
          "`getCachedClipsCount` uses `parseInt` without `Number.isFinite` validation (`clipInitService.ts:38`), so corrupted storage can yield `NaN` while still typed as `number`.",
          "That value feeds skeleton length math in `JoinClipsPage` (`Math.max(2, cachedClipsCount) + 1`), so malformed persistence can alter rendering without any machine-readable degraded signal.",
          "In contrast, similar localStorage-risk code in `useDiscordSignIn` returns structured `operationFailure` with `errorCode` (`useDiscordSignIn.ts:17-24`) and logs metadata."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Normalize this path to explicit degraded signaling: validate parsed counts (`Number.isFinite` + sane bounds), emit a structured recoverable failure/log code on storage errors, and fall back to a deterministic safe count.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Disappeared from scan \u2014 likely fixed",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T00:08:11+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T00:08:11+00:00",
