    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::unchecked_task_update_in_generation_completion::b532965c": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::unchecked_task_update_in_generation_completion::b532965c",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Generation completion performs a DB update without handling write failure",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/complete_task/generation.ts",
          "supabase/functions/complete_task/orchestrator.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "In `handleRegeneration`, `await supabase.from('tasks').update({ generation_created: true }).eq('id', taskId);` (generation.ts lines 331-334) ignores the returned error object entirely.",
          "Sibling code in orchestrator completion checks `updateOrchError` and throws structured `CompletionError` for failed writes (orchestrator.ts lines 569-593 and 633-653)."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Capture `{ error }` from the generation update and throw `toCompletionError`/`CompletionError` with task context when it is non-null, matching the write-failure contract used in orchestrator completion paths.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T00:34:29+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T00:34:29+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-25T00:52:28+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::malformed_json_maps_to_500::252c1850": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::malformed_json_maps_to_500::252c1850",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Invalid request JSON is treated as internal failure instead of client error",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/calculate-task-cost/index.ts",
          "supabase/functions/complete_task/orchestrator.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`calculate-task-cost` uses `const { task_id } = await req.json();` (line 302) inside a broad try/catch; JSON parse failures flow to generic catch (lines 623-629) returning `internal_server_error` (500).",
          "The same function otherwise returns specific client-facing error codes for request issues (e.g., missing `task_id` -> 400 at lines 304-308), so malformed JSON gets a different and less predictable contract."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Wrap `req.json()` in a narrow parse guard and return a deterministic 400 error code (e.g., `invalid_json_body`) before entering downstream task lookup logic.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T00:34:29+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T00:34:29+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-25T00:52:28+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::validation_error_type_eroded_by_broad_catch::8e706111": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::validation_error_type_eroded_by_broad_catch::8e706111",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Task validation errors are normalized away by broad catch-and-wrap blocks",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/imageGeneration.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/joinClips.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/magicEdit.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/tasks/individualTravelSegment.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Each module throws field-aware `TaskValidationError` from validation paths (e.g., imageGeneration.ts lines 204-214, joinClips.ts lines 249-299, magicEdit.ts lines 91-110).",
          "Each task creator then catches all errors and rethrows `handleError(...)` (imageGeneration.ts line 448/530, joinClips.ts line 524, magicEdit.ts lines 219/274, individualTravelSegment.ts line 739), which changes the outward error type and can lose validation-specific shape."
        ],
        "suggestion": "In each `catch`, short-circuit `TaskValidationError` (`if (error instanceof TaskValidationError) throw error;`) and only normalize unexpected/runtime failures via `handleError`.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "not reported in latest holistic re-import",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T00:34:29+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T00:34:29+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-25T00:52:28+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null
    },
