      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Fail-open rate-limit paths still return `ok:false`, conflicting with allow-request semantics.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/_shared/rateLimit.ts",
          "supabase/functions/_shared/edgeOperation.ts",
          "supabase/functions/_shared/edgeRequest.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`checkRateLimit` logs \"allowing request\" and computes `fallback = failOpenRateLimit(...)`, but returns `operationFailure(...)` for RPC/runtime/payload issues (`rateLimit.ts` lines 141-159, 188-195).",
          "In the shared result model, `ok:false` is the canonical failure branch (`edgeOperation.ts` lines 4-24, 50-67), so callers that branch on `ok` will treat fail-open conditions as hard failures.",
          "This creates two parallel meanings of failure (`ok:false` vs `policy:'fail_open'`), increasing caller inconsistency risk at API boundaries."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make fail-open paths return `operationSuccess(fallback, { policy: 'fail_open' })` (or a dedicated degraded-success variant) and reserve `ok:false` for true deny/error paths; update shared helpers so callers can branch consistently on one discriminator.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
