      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Rate-limit retry metadata can become negative and leak to response headers/body.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/_shared/rateLimit.ts",
          "supabase/functions/_shared/edgeRequest.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`checkRateLimit` computes `retryAfter` as `Math.ceil((resetAt.getTime() - now.getTime()) / 1000)` with no lower bound.",
          "`rateLimitResponse` interpolates this value into the message and `Retry-After` header path.",
          "`edgeErrorResponse` serializes `retryAfter` directly when provided."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Clamp `retryAfter` to `Math.max(0, ...)` before returning, and only emit `Retry-After`/retry text when value is > 0 to keep response contracts valid under clock skew or stale reset timestamps.",
