      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "`ok` semantics are inconsistent for degraded failures vs hard failures in edge helpers",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/_shared/rateLimit.ts",
          "supabase/functions/_shared/edgeRequest.ts",
          "supabase/functions/_shared/edgeOperation.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`checkRateLimit` returns `operationSuccess` with `degraded` details when RPC/runtime failures happen (fail-open path).",
          "`parseJsonBody` returns `operationFailure` for invalid body shape/JSON.",
          "Both are `OperationResult`, but `ok` no longer reliably indicates healthy execution vs degraded fallback, forcing endpoint-specific interpretation."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce a shared degraded/fallback contract in `edgeOperation` (for example explicit `state: 'success'|'degraded'|'failure'`) and migrate `checkRateLimit` and request parsing helpers to that contract so `ok` meaning is uniform.",
        "reasoning": ""
