    "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::variant_delay_promise_leak::91fb7414": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::variant_delay_promise_leak::91fb7414",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Debounced variant invalidation can leave earlier callers awaiting forever",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/hooks/invalidation/useGenerationInvalidation.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/timelineWriteQueue.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`waitForVariantDelay` stores one timeout per `generationId`; when a second call arrives it `clearTimeout(existingTimeout)` and deletes the map entry, but the first call's `new Promise` resolve path is never triggered.",
          "Because `invalidateVariantChange` awaits `waitForVariantDelay`, earlier callers can hang indefinitely after being superseded by newer calls.",
          "`runTimelineWriteWithTimeout` in `timelineWriteQueue.ts` shows the opposite contract style: timeout/cancellation paths always settle (throw or return), so callers do not hang."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Change variant-delay dedupe to store and settle waiter state, not just timeout IDs. Keep a per-key record with timeout + resolver, and on supersession either resolve prior waiters immediately (coalesced) or reject them with a typed cancellation error so every call to `invalidateVariantChange` settles.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Disappeared from scan \u2014 likely fixed",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T10:24:11+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T10:24:11+00:00",
