    "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::gallery_navigation_migration_overlap::d13ec5f0": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::gallery_navigation_migration_overlap::d13ec5f0",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Gallery pagination carries both new state machine and legacy control API",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/components/MediaGallery/hooks/useMediaGalleryPagination.ts",
          "src/shared/components/MediaGallery/hooks/useMediaGalleryActions.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`useMediaGalleryPagination` introduces unified `navigationState` but retains backward-compat mutators `setLoadingButton` and `setIsGalleryLoading` (`useMediaGalleryPagination.ts:92-107`, `:195-226`).",
          "The same hook also performs render-time correction via `setTimeout(() => setRawPage(page), 0)` (`useMediaGalleryPagination.ts:121-133`), which is a mechanical workaround rather than a clean state transition boundary.",
          "`useMediaGalleryActions` is another broad behavior bucket (delete/backfill timing, lightbox shaping, download transport, tick UI), amplifying unclear ownership at the gallery hook layer (`useMediaGalleryActions.ts:133-260`)."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Complete the migration by removing legacy setter APIs, move page correction into explicit effect/event transitions, and split `useMediaGalleryActions` into focused hooks (`useGalleryDeleteFlow`, `useGalleryDownload`, `useGalleryLightboxBridge`) aligned with the unified pagination model.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "auto_resolved",
      "note": "Disappeared from scan \u2014 likely fixed",
