        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`checkRateLimit` returns `operationFailure(... errorCode: 'rate_limit_exceeded')` when denied and stores the usable decision payload in `cause.decision` (`supabase/functions/_shared/rateLimit.ts:171-186`).",
          "`rateLimitFailureResponse` must reconstruct a `RateLimitResult` from failure internals (`extractDeniedResultFromFailure`) instead of directly consuming a typed return value (`supabase/functions/_shared/rateLimit.ts:257-289`).",
          "Elsewhere in shared edge request utilities, envelope handling is direct and shape-stable (`edgeErrorResponse`, `parseJsonFailureResponse`), highlighting this divergence (`supabase/functions/_shared/edgeRequest.ts:121-232`)."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Refactor rate-limit checks to return a single typed success payload `{ allowed, remaining, resetAt, retryAfter? }` for both allowed/denied decisions, and reserve `operationFailure` for infrastructure faults (RPC/runtime/parse failures). Keep a thin adapter for existing callers during migration.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
