      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Settings fetch dedupe shares one promise across callers but does not preserve per-caller abort semantics.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/lib/toolSettingsService.ts",
          "src/shared/hooks/invalidation/useGenerationInvalidation.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`fetchToolSettingsSupabase` accepts `signal` but when an identical request is already in-flight it returns `await existingPromise` without signal-aware short-circuit.",
          "Single-flight key excludes cancellation identity, so an aborted caller can remain blocked behind another caller\u2019s request.",
          "In contrast, other coordination code (`waitForVariantDelay`) explicitly resolves coalesced callers, showing this seam currently lacks equivalent cancellation-aware handoff behavior."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Wrap shared in-flight waits with per-caller abort handling (e.g., race shared promise with abort signal), or explicitly remove `signal` from the API if cancellation cannot be honored under dedupe.",
