      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Abort semantics are accepted at the API boundary but not propagated through the async fetch seam, so canceled callers still wait on in-flight work.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "mid_level_elegance",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/lib/toolSettingsService.ts",
          "src/shared/lib/timelineWriteQueue.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`fetchToolSettingsSupabase(..., signal?)` checks `signal.aborted` before start (`toolSettingsService.ts:358-363`) and once before querying (`:380-384`), but does not pass `signal` into `fetchAllScopes` calls (`:386-389`).",
          "If an identical request is already in-flight, the function awaits it unconditionally (`:367-370`) without re-checking caller cancellation.",
          "A contrasting module (`timelineWriteQueue`) uses abort-aware execution with timeout and explicit abort handling (`timelineWriteQueue.ts:54-84`), highlighting inconsistency at integration seams."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Honor cancellation end-to-end: thread `AbortSignal` through scope fetches (or race with an abort promise), and short-circuit coalesced callers on abort while leaving shared work for non-aborted callers.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Threaded AbortSignal through scope fetches, added raceWithAbort for single-flight waits, and enforced abort checks at each async seam.",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T17:35:53+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T17:35:53+00:00",
