    "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::orchestrator_prop_bag_timeline_lightbox::dcd2ef2a": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::orchestrator_prop_bag_timeline_lightbox::dcd2ef2a",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Timeline and gallery lightbox rely on oversized pass-through contracts that blur ownership boundaries.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/Timeline.tsx",
          "src/shared/components/MediaGallery/components/MediaGalleryLightbox.tsx",
          "src/shared/components/MediaLightbox/ImageLightbox.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`Timeline.tsx` declares a large `TimelineProps` contract and forwards many of those props almost directly into `TimelineContainer` and `MediaLightbox`, mixing domain orchestration with view wiring.",
          "`MediaGalleryLightbox.tsx` groups props into many sub-contracts but still performs navigation-state computation, query-cache subscription, task prefetching, shot workflow, and modal handoff in one component.",
          "`ImageLightbox.tsx` consumes broad grouped props (`navigation`, `shotWorkflow`, `features`, `actions`) and then reconstructs another large call into `useSharedLightboxState`, extending the pass-through chain."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Split orchestration into focused adapters per concern (navigation adapter, shot workflow adapter, task-details adapter) and pass only feature-local props to each rendered subtree. Move `MediaLightbox`/`TimelineContainer` dependency assembly into dedicated hooks that expose narrow, concern-specific contracts.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Reduced timeline/lightbox pass-through orchestration by introducing useTimelineDomainService and useTimelineLightboxOrchestrator in Timeline.tsx, and by converting MediaGalleryLightbox to grouped contracts plus focused controller hooks that own navigation and generation-lookup adapters.",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T20:18:32+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T20:18:32+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-25T20:41:36+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
        "text": "I have actually narrowed the orchestration surfaces in Timeline and MediaGalleryLightbox and I am not gaming the score by resolving without fixing.",
        "attested_at": "2026-02-25T20:41:36+00:00",
        "scan_verified": false
      }
    },
    "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::hook_surface_overcomposition::5106a310": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::hook_surface_overcomposition::5106a310",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "High-indirection hook APIs create low-leverage abstraction layers and rigid caller choreography.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/components/MediaLightbox/hooks/useSharedLightboxState.ts",
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/Timeline/hooks/useTimelineActionHandlers.ts",
          "src/tools/travel-between-images/components/Timeline/hooks/useTimelineViewportController.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`useSharedLightboxState.ts` composes many prop sub-interfaces into one mega-input plus a large nested return model, so small feature changes require touching broad contracts.",
          "`useTimelineActionHandlers.ts` requires multiple pipeline objects (`dropPipeline`, `duplicatePipeline`, `tapToMovePipeline`, `structureVideoPipeline`, `endpointPipeline`) with many fields, indicating the abstraction is coordinating too many subsystems at once.",
          "`useTimelineViewportController.ts` similarly bundles dimensions/refs/drag orchestration and timing guards in one hook, increasing hidden coupling between zoom, drag lifecycle, and frame geometry behavior."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Refactor these hooks into smaller single-purpose hooks with explicit composition at the call site (e.g., `useTimelineDropActions`, `useTimelineEndpointActions`, `useLightboxShotState`, `useLightboxVariantState`) and keep each hook\u2019s input focused on one concern boundary.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Split several cross-cutting hook responsibilities: extracted Timeline lightbox orchestration into useTimelineLightboxOrchestrator, moved shot action intent logic into useShotActionController, and decomposed MediaGalleryLightbox behavior via dedicated controller hooks for navigation, shot-association, task payload, and generation navigation.",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T20:18:32+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T20:18:32+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-25T20:41:31+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
        "text": "I have actually extracted and rewired these responsibilities into focused hooks and I am not gaming the score by resolving without fixing.",
        "attested_at": "2026-02-25T20:41:31+00:00",
        "scan_verified": false
      }
    },
    "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::edge_handler_flow_duplication::4b00fb11": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::design_coherence::edge_handler_flow_duplication::4b00fb11",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 3,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Edge functions duplicate request choreography despite shared primitives, causing structural drift.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "supabase/functions/generate-upload-url/index.ts",
          "supabase/functions/get-task-output/index.ts",
          "supabase/functions/setup-auto-topup/index.ts",
          "supabase/functions/update-shot-pair-prompts/index.ts",
          "supabase/functions/_shared/edgeRequest.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Each handler uses `bootstrapEdgeHandler` (or equivalent shared runtime utilities) but still re-implements similar method/body validation, auth branching, logging flush points, and error response shaping inline.",
          "Response styles diverge across siblings (plain-text error bodies vs JSON envelopes), even for similar validation/auth failures, which indicates inconsistent handler-level conventions.",
          "`update-shot-pair-prompts/index.ts` includes request parsing, ownership checks, filtering policy, and mutation loop in a single route body, combining domain policy and transport concerns."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Introduce reusable handler composition for common edge flows (auth policy, validation policy, response serializer, ownership guard) and keep each route focused on domain-specific data operations. Standardize one response envelope strategy for sibling functions.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Standardized edge handler choreography by migrating generate-upload-url/get-task-output/update-shot-pair-prompts onto bootstrapEdgeHandler + jsonResponse, reducing per-route auth/body/method boilerplate and aligning error envelope behavior; setup-auto-topup already follows same stack.",
      "first_seen": "2026-02-25T20:18:32+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-02-25T20:18:32+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-02-25T20:41:25+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
