    "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::join_clips_global_queue_unscoped::f3b59550": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::join_clips_global_queue_unscoped::f3b59550",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Join Clips handoff is coupled through a single unscoped mutable global queue (`localStorage.pendingJoinClips`), allowing cross-project/session contamination and non-deterministic startup behavior.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "src/shared/components/MediaLightbox/hooks/useJoinClips.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/lib/clipInitService.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useClipManager.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`useJoinClips` appends payloads to hard-coded key `pendingJoinClips` without project/user scope (`localStorage.setItem('pendingJoinClips', ...)`).",
          "`consumePendingJoinClips` reads from the same global key and clears it (`localStorage.removeItem(PENDING_CLIPS_KEY)`), with no projectId filter in payload schema.",
          "`useClipManager` consumes this queue independently of project identity (`useEffect` depends on `settingsLoaded` only), so queue consumption is not tied to explicit route/project initialization contracts."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace the global key queue with a scoped registry (`pendingJoinClips:<projectId>:<userId>`) or move handoff to a typed in-app store/query cache keyed by project. Make producer and consumer share one typed contract module and require `projectId` at write/consume boundaries.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Replaced global pending queue contract with scoped keys by project and user via a shared pending-queue contract module; producer and consumer now share typed entry and queue-key helpers, and useClipManager consumes with explicit selectedProjectId boundary.",
      "first_seen": "2026-03-02T10:11:09+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-02T10:11:09+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-03-02T10:31:01+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
        "text": "I have actually Replaced global pending queue contract with scoped keys by project and user via a shared pending-queue contract module; producer and consumer now share typed entry and queue-key helpers, and useClipManager consumes with explicit selectedProjectId boundary. and I am not gaming the score.",
        "attested_at": "2026-03-02T10:31:01+00:00",
        "scan_verified": false
      }
    },
    "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::join_clips_hydration_persist_race::9554ade5": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::join_clips_hydration_persist_race::9554ade5",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Join Clips can overwrite persisted clip settings with empty state before hydration completes due to effect ordering and missing hydration gate.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useClipManager.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useJoinClipsSettings.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`useClipManager` starts with `clips=[]` and has a persist effect that runs whenever `settingsLoaded` is true (`lines 146-165`), serializing and calling `joinSettings.updateFields` if different.",
          "Hydration effect (`lines 111-141`) may set clips asynchronously after poster preloading; during that window persist effect can compare existing saved clips against empty `clipsToSave` and write empty values.",
          "No guard like `hasHydratedInitialState`/`isHydrating` is checked in the persist effect before writing."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Add an explicit hydration phase flag and block persistence until initial settings hydration (and preload path) completes. Alternatively collapse hydrate+persist into a single reducer/state machine with explicit `UNINITIALIZED -> HYDRATED -> DIRTY` transitions.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Added explicit initial hydration-complete gating in useClipManager and blocked persistence effects until hydration finishes (including poster-preload path), so startup empty clips state cannot overwrite persisted settings before hydration resolves.",
      "first_seen": "2026-03-02T10:11:09+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-02T10:11:09+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-03-02T10:31:14+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
        "text": "I have actually Added explicit initial hydration-complete gating in useClipManager and blocked persistence effects until hydration finishes (including poster-preload path), so startup empty clips state cannot overwrite persisted settings before hydration resolves. and I am not gaming the score.",
        "attested_at": "2026-03-02T10:31:14+00:00",
        "scan_verified": false
      }
    },
    "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::pending_queue_consumed_before_project_binding::2a746688": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::pending_queue_consumed_before_project_binding::2a746688",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Pending Join Clips queue can be consumed and cleared before target project binding stabilizes, causing dropped queued work on project transitions.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "initialization_coupling",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useClipManager.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/lib/clipInitService.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/pages/JoinClipsPage.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Queue consume effect runs on `[settingsLoaded]` only (`useClipManager` lines 90-106), not on `selectedProjectId`.",
          "Project change reset effect (`lines 76-85`) clears in-memory clips; consumed queue entries are not replayable because `consumePendingJoinClips` removes storage key once read (`clipInitService` line 272).",
          "This creates a workflow blind spot: packet/work item (pending clip action) is generated and then dropped if consumption happens before the final project context is settled."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Gate queue consumption on a stable `selectedProjectId` and include projectId in queue entries. Only clear consumed entries after they are bound to the same project context and merged successfully; keep unmatched entries for later drain.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Gated pending-queue consumption on stable selectedProjectId and propagated project scope into consumePendingJoinClips; queue entries now include project/user scope and consumers filter by matching scope before merge, preventing early cross-project drain/clear during project transitions.",
      "first_seen": "2026-03-02T10:11:09+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-03-02T10:11:09+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-03-02T10:31:10+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "lang": "typescript",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
        "text": "I have actually Gated pending-queue consumption on stable selectedProjectId and propagated project scope into consumePendingJoinClips; queue entries now include project/user scope and consumers filter by matching scope before merge, preventing early cross-project drain/clear during project transitions. and I am not gaming the score.",
        "attested_at": "2026-03-02T10:31:10+00:00",
