        "evidence": [
          "`taskParamsUtils.ts` defines custom source orders (`TRAVEL_SEGMENT_IMAGE_SOURCE_ORDER`, `TRAVEL_TIMELINE_IMAGE_SOURCE_ORDER`, `TRAVEL_PROMPT_SOURCE_ORDER`) and calls `createTravelPayloadReader` directly with those arrays.",
          "`travelContractData.ts` independently defines `CONTRACT_SOURCES` and `LEGACY_SOURCES`, with a different legacy order (`orchestratorDetails`, `rawParams`, `fullOrchestratorPayload`) and separate fallback logic.",
          "`individualTravelSegment.ts` consumes `readTravelContractData(snapshot)` while other UI paths call `deriveInputImages`/`derivePrompt`, so equivalent fields can resolve differently depending on caller."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Create one canonical travel payload selector contract (single module exporting field-level precedence tables and typed selectors), then migrate `taskParamsUtils`, `travelContractData`, and segment/task-detail consumers to that shared selector API.",
