        "evidence": [
          "`waitForVariantDelay` resolves superseded callers via `settleCallbacks.forEach(settle)` after clearing prior timeout.",
          "`invalidateVariantChange` immediately continues after awaited delay resolution and performs invalidations/refetches, so superseded calls still run.",
          "Current test checks that superseded promise settles, but does not assert that only latest invalidation side effects fire."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Change delay coalescing to cancellation semantics (e.g., resolve with `superseded` sentinel and early-return in `invalidateVariantChange`) and add test assertions on invalidate/refetch call counts for superseded callers.",
        "reasoning": ""
