      "summary": "Play-event listeners are added per clip without effective cleanup",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useClipManager.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/components/SortableClip.tsx",
          "src/tools/join-clips/pages/JoinClipsPage.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "In `useClipManager.ts`, the effect that iterates `clips` adds `video.addEventListener('play', preventPlay)` but returns cleanup from inside `forEach`, so React never receives those cleanups.",
          "As clips change, listeners can accumulate on reused video elements, creating hidden behavior coupling and potential performance/logic drift."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Collect listener cleanup functions in an array and return one top-level cleanup function from the effect; alternatively attach this behavior at the `SortableClip` element level with proper mount/unmount cleanup per video element.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
