        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`MediaGalleryLightbox.tsx` subscribes directly to `queryClient.getQueryCache()` and bumps local `cacheVersion` on broad `updated` events.",
          "The memoized media enhancement explicitly references `void cacheVersion` just to force recomputation, which is an implicit rerender trigger rather than explicit data dependency.",
          "This couples component behavior to low-level cache event mechanics and broad query-key matching, making behavior hard to reason about as cache usage evolves."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Replace manual cache subscription with explicit query selectors (`useQuery`/derived hook) keyed to the active generation/task mapping, and propagate optimistic starred updates through typed mutation updaters instead of global cache-event listeners.",
        "reasoning": ""
