          "src/domains/generation/hooks/useDeleteGenerationWithConfirm.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`DeleteGenerationConfirmContract` defines `onConfirm: () => void` only.",
          "`ConfirmDialog` supports `onConfirm: () => void | Promise<void>` plus `isLoading`.",
          "`DeleteGenerationConfirmDialog` re-exports the narrow contract and cannot pass loading state.",
          "Consumers therefore split behavior inconsistently (`isPending` boolean in travel view vs `deletingId` in gallery/join-clips), because dialog-level contract cannot represent in-flight confirm semantics."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Promote a single confirm contract used by both base and delete dialogs: include async `onConfirm` and explicit pending state (`isConfirming`), then thread it through `useDeleteGenerationWithConfirm` and all call sites so delete UX and API shape are consistent.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Unified delete confirmation contract around async onConfirm plus explicit pending state (isConfirming), threaded through DeleteGenerationConfirmDialog/useDeleteGenerationWithConfirm, and aligned delete action to async mutateAsync flow with coherent loading semantics.",
