        "dimension": "api_surface_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/join-clips/lib/clipInitService.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useClipManager.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/lib/__tests__/clipInitService.test.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "Docstring says each action is `{ type: 'fill' | 'append', clip }` (`clipInitService.ts:196-203`).",
          "Actual exported type is `PendingClipAction { clip: VideoClip }` without `type` (`204-206`).",
          "Placement decision is deferred to `applyPendingClipActions` (`315-349`), so API callers cannot reason about intent from the returned contract."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make the contract honest in one direction: either return a true discriminated union with explicit `type`, or update docs/types to explicitly state action placement is resolved only by `applyPendingClipActions` and keep both functions as a single cohesive API surface.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Made PendingClipAction explicit as deferred_insert; corrected consume/apply contract docs; updated join-clips tests for deferred action shape; validated with focused vitest and strict typecheck.",
