          "src/shared/lib/tasks/__tests__/taskParamContract.test.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`extractTaskParamBoolean` treats any number as boolean by `value === 1`; non-1 numbers become `false` (`taskParamContract.ts:123-131`).",
          "`extractAddInPositionParam` then defaults null to false (`157-159`), so malformed values and explicit false collapse to the same result.",
          "Tests only cover `0` and `1` encodings (`taskParamContract.test.ts:43-48`), leaving undefined behavior for malformed numeric values."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Tighten contract parsing: accept only `0|1` for numeric boolean encodings, return `null` for other numbers, and let `extractAddInPositionParam` surface/telemetry invalid payloads before defaulting.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Tightened boolean task-param parsing to accept numeric encodings only for 0/1, added invalid add_in_position telemetry before fallback, and added direct tests for invalid numeric payloads.",
