          "src/shared/lib/__tests__/timelineWriteQueue.test.ts"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "`runSerializedTimelineWrite` waits on `previousTail` with no queue-level timeout or circuit breaker, so unresolved tasks block the shot queue indefinitely.",
          "Timeouts are optional and caller-managed (`runTimelineWriteWithTimeout`), but queue entry does not require/verify timeout-wrapped tasks.",
          "Existing tests cover ordering and timeout helper behavior, not queue recovery when a queued task never resolves."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Make timeout/abort enforcement part of the queue contract: add a required per-task timeout (or wrapper overload) in `runSerializedTimelineWrite`, emit a terminal queue event on timeout, and add tests for blocked-first-write + second-write recovery behavior.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "Added a queue-level watchdog timeout to runSerializedTimelineWrite so a hung per-shot task cannot block the queue indefinitely, with tests proving timed-out writes release the queue and allow follow-up writes to run.",
