      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "summary": "Scroll-state effect creates timers that are never cleared because cleanup is returned from the event handler instead of the effect.",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "design_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/tools/join-clips/hooks/useClipManager.ts",
          "src/tools/join-clips/pages/JoinClipsPage.tsx"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "In `useClipManager`, `handleScroll` returns `() => clearTimeout(timer)` (`useClipManager.ts:304-307`), but DOM listeners ignore returned values from handlers.",
          "Effect cleanup only removes the listener (`useClipManager.ts:309-310`), so rapid scroll events queue many outstanding timers and delayed state updates.",
          "`JoinClipsPage` depends on `isScrolling` for drag/drop behavior, so timer churn directly affects UI interaction consistency."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Store timer id in a ref and clear/restart it inside `handleScroll`; clear it in effect cleanup alongside removing the listener.",
        "reasoning": ""
      },
      "status": "fixed",
